# Saved weights from stage 3. Quick-mode fits are smoke-test noise; the
# full-mode .npz is ~2 KB and worth committing, since it lets anyone
# regenerate the end-to-end figure without a GPU.
docs/examples/wppm/fits/hong2025_quick_fit.npz

# Same split for the NUTS example. The documentation is written from
# --mode balanced, so plots/nuts_*_balanced.* and fits/nuts_balanced_fit.npz
# are committed: with the cached fit, `--from-fit` regenerates every figure and
# every printed diagnostic on the page without a GPU. Quick mode writes the
# unsuffixed names, which are smoke-test output and must never be mistaken for
# the figures the docs embed.
docs/examples/wppm/fits/nuts_quick_fit.npz
